          "subComponents": [
            {
              "description": {
                "type": "textComponent",
                "text": "The Web Development Immersive course at General Assembly was a great start to the world of development. It’s an intensive three-month full-time course, taught by industry experts that covers a wide array of languages and skills but also is taught based around TDD, daily standups, pair programming and presenting code to emulate working practices within the industry.  During the course we produced 4 main projects, 3 on our own and 1 as a team:\n\nProject 4 - iWish\nhttps://iwish.jwlh.co.uk\n\nTech: MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js, AWS file upload, Axios, Bcrypt, Bootstrap, Lodash, Nodemailer, Mailgun, Bluebird, Mocha, Chai.\n\nProject 4 was our final project in which we were tasked with building a full MERN stack application. As it was also in the lead up to Christmas I chose to create a wishlist app enabling users to create a wishlist and share it with their friends and family.  \n\nProject 3 - HappyCabby\nhttps://happycabby-jonny.herokuapp.com/\n\nTech: MongoDB, Express.js, Angular, Node.js, Mocha, Chai, Bluebird, JWT tokens, Bulma, Bcrypt.\n\nWorking in a team we produced a full MEAN stack application. We also used several APIs including Google Maps, Geocode and Eventful’s API.\n\nHappy Cabby is an application designed to show taxi drivers what events are happening around them and how busy those events are so that they can where will be busy.\n \nProject 2 - Eat Better Pizza\nhttps://eat-better-pizza.herokuapp.com/\n\nTech: MongoDB, Express.js, EJS Layouts, Bluebird, Bcrypt.\n\nEat Better Pizza is a full-stack RESTful app using Express.js, EJS Layouts, SASS, BCrypt & a Mongo database.\n\nAllowing users to sign up, create reviews of restaurants and comment on existing ones, all to make sure they are eating the best pizza possible!\n\nProject 1 - Simon The Synth\nhttps://simon-the-synth.herokuapp.com/\n\nTech: HTML, CSS & JavaScript/jQuery.\n\nThe first project on the course was to build a game using HTML, CSS & JavaScript/jQuery.  I decided to create a SIMON game based on a retro synth pad."
              }
